1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,420
Before adding lots of rewards,

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,540
what should we decide to keep progression coherent?

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:09,220
We will use the ammunition and research in Wizard with a Gun

4
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:12,040
to separate functions, conditions and limits on power,

5
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:16,660
then examine production scope through
ranching actions in Cult of the Lamb.

6
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:18,520
By the end, you will be able to record a reward's

7
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,420
function, conditions and required work

8
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,000
together in one catalogue row.

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,900
Let us begin with ammunition that freezes enemies

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,740
and ammunition that creates a path.

11
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,230
Let us first examine functions in this
official ammunition demonstration.

12
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:30,810
Watch an enemy freeze after a shot,

13
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:34,130
then ice shatter in a separate combat cut.

14
00:00:38,302 --> 00:00:41,822
Next, the character crosses a gap using created ground.

15
00:00:42,082 --> 00:00:44,842
The change concerns a way to move, beyond a damage number.

16
00:00:45,688 --> 00:00:46,928
The ammunition selection also describes

17
00:00:46,928 --> 00:00:48,288
healing living targets

18
00:00:48,288 --> 00:00:50,848
and attacking undead targets differently.

19
00:00:51,697 --> 00:00:55,097
These are separately edited shots, so they
cannot establish a numerical power comparison.

20
00:00:55,377 --> 00:00:58,657
We are distinguishing the actions
each ammunition type changes.

21
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:04,790
In the initial catalogue, record the action that
changes after acquisition before naming the item.

22
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:08,170
Separate power increases, new options,

23
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:11,330
and rewards for expression or
collecting. This reveals missing roles.

24
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:15,890
A proposed decoration or keepsake
is a candidate in our own design,

25
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:18,210
not a claim that it exists in the shown game.

26
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:20,130
First establish why it is needed.

27
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:23,527
The demonstration separately shows
picking up materials near enemies

28
00:01:23,527 --> 00:01:27,007
and selecting branches at a research station.

29
00:01:31,924 --> 00:01:33,904
It then shows furnace inputs and outputs,

30
00:01:33,904 --> 00:01:36,724
and the listed requirements for crafting ammunition.

31
00:01:40,894 --> 00:01:44,954
The potion interface changes selection
from the weaker potion to the next entry.

32
00:01:45,294 --> 00:01:48,814
Yet a missing-ingredients message
remains alongside a completed state.

33
00:01:49,148 --> 00:01:51,128
Another trailer separately shows bounty pickups,

34
00:01:51,128 --> 00:01:55,268
interaction with the reward
machine, and a weapon pickup prompt.

35
00:01:55,568 --> 00:01:58,656
These also give us questions about conditions at each stage.

36
00:01:58,656 --> 00:02:03,463
This promotional edit cannot prove a
normal payment or acquisition process.

37
00:02:03,683 --> 00:02:08,063
Use the observation to record research,
crafting and actual use as separate steps.

38
00:02:08,583 --> 00:02:12,083
For each reward, record when it becomes
available, what must precede it,

39
00:02:12,083 --> 00:02:15,143
and what must still be crafted before use.

40
00:02:15,523 --> 00:02:19,563
Check whether another route can bypass the previous step,

41
00:02:19,563 --> 00:02:22,743
and whether the required materials
are available at that point.

42
00:02:23,003 --> 00:02:26,543
Leave acquisition conditions not
established by the footage unverified.

43
00:02:27,023 --> 00:02:31,603
Turn the gap into a question for our own
design instead of filling it with assumptions.

44
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:34,510
These shots show water and electrical combat effects,

45
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:36,850
collecting an ice-related material,

46
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:39,350
and selecting a lightning research entry.

47
00:02:45,350 --> 00:02:49,810
In the next cuts, several effects and several
players' attacks overlap in one space.

48
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:53,370
One added function can require more than one test situation.

49
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:57,450
Some ammunition changes role depending
on its target, as with healing,

50
00:02:57,450 --> 00:03:00,930
so a single damage ranking is insufficient for the catalogue.

51
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:04,710
Watch the purple circular effect spread
and several enemies approach in other cuts.

52
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:08,590
We can list the targets to test when areas of effect overlap.

53
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:11,850
The footage does not establish poor balance.

54
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:16,710
We are extracting questions about
combinations and targets for our own design.

55
00:03:17,350 --> 00:03:19,810
If growth is central, plan the range of power increases.

56
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:25,430
If equal competition is central, examine whether
accumulated upgrades undermine that goal.

57
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:28,770
The cooperative game we just saw is not
being presented as a competitive game.

58
00:03:28,950 --> 00:03:32,310
This is a proposal to set caps, simultaneous-use
rules and replacement conditions

59
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:34,110
for the intended experience.

60
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:38,770
For each new reward, list situations
where it combines with existing entries.

61
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:43,330
Then decide whether to adjust numbers
or preserve a trade-off between choices.

62
00:03:44,067 --> 00:03:50,387
The Cult of the Lamb ranch shows
petting, milking and feeding selections.

63
00:03:52,307 --> 00:03:54,927
Other shots show riding an animal, moving and dismounting.

64
00:03:57,399 --> 00:04:00,179
Now look at the wizard's appearance settings.

65
00:04:00,399 --> 00:04:01,879
After clothing and masks are changed,

66
00:04:01,879 --> 00:04:05,379
separate shots show differently dressed characters moving.

67
00:04:06,403 --> 00:04:10,383
Production and movement should not be grouped
under the same function as changing appearance.

68
00:04:10,663 --> 00:04:17,963
These edits do not establish animal
unlock conditions or clothing statistics.

69
00:04:18,203 --> 00:04:20,103
Record appearance and function separately.

70
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:23,993
Customization, records and
collectibles can be reward candidates.

71
00:04:24,373 --> 00:04:27,613
Quantity alone does not make them necessary.

72
00:04:28,113 --> 00:04:31,093
Separate purposes such as expression, commemorating play,

73
00:04:31,393 --> 00:04:34,633
and enabling new production or movement.

74
00:04:35,113 --> 00:04:37,913
Two visually different entries may also differ functionally.

75
00:04:38,453 --> 00:04:43,693
Separate appearance from function to avoid confusing
pure customization with added capabilities.

76
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:48,370
Back in Wizard with a Gun, watch floor cells being added

77
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:51,890
and distinct workstations and objects being placed.

78
00:04:53,730 --> 00:04:59,070
After the placement shots, combat shows ice, fire
and electrical effects overlapping different actions.

79
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:03,890
A blue projectile is followed by orange explosions
and circular ground effects in separate shots.

80
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:07,810
These visible differences suggest
presentation work from firing through impact.

81
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:10,610
Player material costs are conditions inside the game.

82
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:14,160
Creating those appearances and behaviors is development work.

83
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:17,410
We do not know the developer's actual budget or code.

84
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:21,350
Use the visible differences to consider the images, behaviors

85
00:05:21,350 --> 00:05:23,190
and combinations our own entries require.

86
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:28,470
Next to each catalogue row, list icons,
models or drawings, animation, effects,

87
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:30,770
interface guidance and test situations.

88
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:34,670
Distinguishing reusable assets from new work

89
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:36,850
turns the catalogue into a production scope.

90
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:38,950
This table is our planning tool.

91
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:43,210
Record responsibilities and missing
conditions before inventing precise costs,

92
00:05:43,210 --> 00:05:45,630
then produce manageable groups of entries.

93
00:05:46,367 --> 00:05:48,167
Across these distinct combat shots,

94
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:52,167
pick a target and surrounding
environment in which an effect appears.

95
00:05:52,787 --> 00:05:55,187
Ask which enemies and terrain a
new ammunition type should address,

96
00:05:55,187 --> 00:05:59,447
and where it connects to collecting materials and returning.

97
00:06:05,367 --> 00:06:08,787
The cooperative shot includes other players' actions.

98
00:06:08,927 --> 00:06:13,647
A reward's checklist can distinguish
solo use from use alongside others.

99
00:06:13,887 --> 00:06:18,047
Turn also to Cult of the Lamb combat
in snowy areas and on brick floors.

100
00:06:18,047 --> 00:06:22,587
Enemy sizes, ground markings and
incoming attack patterns visibly differ.

101
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:25,167
In front of a large enemy, we can see the wind-up

102
00:06:25,167 --> 00:06:28,267
followed by a spreading red attack.

103
00:06:28,747 --> 00:06:32,727
We should test a new reward during preparation
and avoidance as well as at impact.

104
00:06:32,927 --> 00:06:38,287
Whether the same combat effect remains readable in
other terrain is another question for our own test list.

105
00:06:38,707 --> 00:06:41,847
We are not guessing rules the footage fails to establish.

106
00:06:42,247 --> 00:06:46,367
We are turning observed actions into
review questions for our own catalogue.

107
00:06:49,717 --> 00:06:52,817
Pick one reward and connect its
changed action, acquisition conditions,

108
00:06:52,817 --> 00:06:56,677
constrained combinations and
required production work in one row.

109
00:06:56,837 --> 00:07:00,757
If many fields are empty, decide those
conditions before adding more items.

110
00:07:01,017 --> 00:07:04,977
If one role repeats, consider
candidates serving another purpose.

111
00:07:05,257 --> 00:07:09,777
A useful starting point is one explainable reward row.

112
00:07:09,977 --> 00:07:13,697
Check that row against both actual
play and the work needed to produce it.
